 "result": "I created a `Dockerfile` and a `.dockerignore` in the repository root. I couldn't build or run the image here, so neither file has been tested. No existing file was changed.\n\nThe runtime only reads `VERSION` from the repo, so the `.dockerignore` exclusions (specs, docs, swagger) are safe.\n\n**What the Dockerfile does**\n- **Build stage:** it starts from `ruby:4.0.6-slim`, the version in `.ruby-version`. It compiles the native gems and skips the development, test and rerun groups.\n- **Runtime stage:** it installs `wireguard-tools`, `iproute2`, `iptables`, `bash` and `openresolv`. It copies in the gems and the app, and sets `ENVIRONMENT=production` and `PORT=3000`. It runs `bundle exec puma config.ru`.\n- **Bash as `/bin/sh`:** `server_config_updater.rb` runs `wg syncconf wg0 <(wg-quick strip wg0)` through `Kernel.system`. That is bash-only syntax, so I linked `/bin/sh` to bash in the image.\n- **Ports and storage:** it exposes 3000/tcp for the API and 51820/udp for WireGuard. `/etc/wireguard` is a volume, since that is where `wg0.conf` and `wg0.json` live.\n- **Health check:** it calls `/healthz` using Ruby, because curl isn't installed.\n\n**Running the container**\n- Set `AUTH_TOKEN` (or `AUTH_DIGEST_TOKEN`) and `WG_HOST`.\n- Add `--cap-add=NET_ADMIN` (plus `SYS_MODULE` if the kernel module has to be loaded).\n- Set the sysctls `net.ipv4.ip_forward=1`, `net.ipv4.conf.all.src_valid_mark=1` and `net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding=1`.\n- A full `docker run` example is in the comments at the bottom of the Dockerfile.\n\n**Files created**\n- `Dockerfile`\n- `.dockerignore`",
